# spark -- the tale behind `spark lua`: O Urubu-Rei e a Lua, a retelling of
# a Karaja tale of how night and day began. A block is a [tag] line, then
# the English, then the Portuguese; blank lines and # lines are ignored.
# [1]..[8] are the eight memories: pieces of one line of the tale, in
# order, assembled as the hero collects them. Your own copy in
# ~/.config/spark/tale is read before this one.

[abertura]
In the beginning of the Karajá people's time there was no Sun, no Moon and no Stars.
No início do tempo do povo Karajá, não havia o Sol, nem a Lua e nem as Estrelas.

[1]
He remembered the river,
Ele lembrou do rio,

[2]
the forest,
da mata,

[3]
the hunt,
da caçada,

[4]
the wind,
do vento,

[5]
the rain,
da chuva,

[6]
the thunder
do trovão

[7]
and the lightning,
e do raio,

[8]
and his body filled with a strength he had forgotten.
e seu corpo foi se enchendo de uma força que ele havia esquecido.

[queda]
Some say not even the great hero escaped Sloth.
Alguns dizem que nem o grande herói foi capaz de escapar da Preguiça.

[fim]
From Cananxiué's body I will blow the Stars across the sky, and Tahiná will be the Evening Star of the Karajá.
Do corpo de Cananxiué vou soprar as Estrelas do firmamento, e Tahiná será a Estrela Vespertina dos Karajás.
